      fix: stop reading `when` after a list pattern as its designation (#467)
      
      `path switch { [var background] when Is(background, "background") => 1 }`
      was an ERROR node. A list pattern may carry a designation (`[1, 2] list`),
      and the designation rule's precedence made the parser shift `when` as that
      designation instead of reducing the pattern and starting the `when_clause`.
      
      The designation-less list pattern now has precedence 2 and the designated
      one precedence 1, as separate productions over a shared
      `_list_pattern_body`, so only the `when` lookahead changes and
      `[1, 2] list` still binds. The `[list_pattern, collection_expression]`
      conflict becomes `[_list_pattern_body, collection_expression]`. Generated
      files regenerated with tree-sitter-cli 0.26.5.
      
      Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
