      fix(csharp): address review of the v0.24.0 grammar bump
      
      Parser (Parse_csharp_tree_sitter.ml):
      - Preprocessor conditionals keep every #if/#elif/#else branch at all
        sites (top level, declarations, initializers, collections, attribute
        lists, enum members, function bodies, else statements, expressions,
        return tails); expression sites become a Conditional chain on an
        opaque #if condition.
      - Primary constructors: class, struct and record parameters stay in
        cparams only (no synthetic public fields); `: Base(args)` arguments
        are kept in cextends.
      - Recursive patterns keep the type name of `Dog(var x) d` (PatTyped),
        property clauses become PatRecord, and parenthesized/list patterns
        keep their designation. Collection spread is Call(Special Spread).
      - C# 14 file-based app directives (`#:package Name@1.0`, ...) become
        `Pragma (kind, [name; value])`; `#!` becomes a Shebang directive.
      
      Grammar (semgrep-c-sharp wrapper, parser regenerated):
      - `#:` directives are top-level items instead of extras.
      - Enum members inside #if may carry their own commas.
      - Pattern syntax: `$...X` in collections, `...` in list patterns and
        extension blocks, standalone `extension($T $X) { ... }` (with
        `extension` still usable as an identifier) and lone `case P: ...`
        (Partial PartialSwitchCase).
      
      Analysis and matching:
      - AST_to_IL lowers `a?.f = rhs` to `if (a != null) a.f = rhs`, so the
        write reaches `a` while staying a weak update.
      - Container elements accept a metavariable ellipsis; list patterns
        accept `...`.
      
      Tests: new rule/pattern tests for each item; AST snapshots of the new
      C# parsing tests now live next to them as tests/parsing/csharp/*.ast.expect.
